# Festag — dark-mode CTAs (Forest Intelligence)

In **dark / Forest** auth and onboarding chrome, idle CTAs stay quiet; ready primary flips to deep Festag blue.

## Geometry

Auth CTAs and fields use **`--festag-auth-radius: 14px`**.

- CTAs / inputs: `14px`
- Icon buttons: `--festag-auth-radius-sm` / `12px`
- Textareas: `--festag-auth-radius-lg` / `16px`
- Cards / popups: `20px`
- **Not** marketing pills (`999px`) and **not** portal-dense `8px`

## Idle (empty / invalid / not ready)

Quiet transparent secondary language:

```css
background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
color: #C7D0CC;
border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
border-radius: var(--festag-auth-radius, 14px);
```

## Ready (valid input → `--ready`)

Only the **primary** action flips to deep Festag blue:

```css
background: linear-gradient(180deg, #3B6BFF 0%, #295CFF 100%);
color: #F5F8F6;
border: 1px solid transparent;
box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(41, 92, 255, 0.18), 0 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.22);
```

Hover `#3B6BFF` / active `#234DE0`. Ghost / secondary stay at idle density.

## Portal primary

Portal / Execution dark primaries use the same deep blue (not soft cool-white).

## Do not

- Soft cool-white `#F0F2F5` ready CTAs in dark
- Make idle primary and ready primary look the same
- Force `--ready` on empty invite / incomplete emails
- Give ghost the ready blue fill
- Reintroduce pure `#000` canvas or pure `#fff` body ink
- Reintroduce full-pill `border-radius:999px` on auth CTAs/inputs

See also `festag-light-mode-ctas.mdc` (light stays white fills) and `festag-night-dark.mdc`.
